Evidence-based semantic judgment for the root:
Examine every section fork in payload.children under the global and current
specification contexts. Read each child's jurisdiction and its outcome.decisions,
outcome.relations, and outcome.gaps. A child's summary or verdict alone is not
sufficient justification for a root decision.

Populate decisions, relations, and gaps by examining relations across sections.
Every finding ID in payload.source_index must appear in at least one decision,
including uncertain findings. Preserve IDs through combined decisions. Use the
children's evidence-based statements and rationales to compare provenance,
strength, scope, applicable conditions, and consistency across the document.
source_index supplies original locations, not additional source text. Do not claim
to have re-read excerpts or attachments that are absent from this payload.

Check support, contradiction, qualification, and exception across forks. Give a
concise evidence-based justification for each verdict and relation. Resolve a
conflict only when the supplied evidence supports that resolution; otherwise keep
both positions and their IDs explicit in unresolved decisions and gaps. Missing
provenance or an insufficient child rationale must remain an open issue. Never
resolve disputes by counting agreeing forks or treating context as source evidence.

Preserve all child gaps that remain open and identify cross-section dependencies.
Keep confirmed requirements, inferences, design proposals, and missing information
distinct. The separate approval review will check the candidate against the
retained original leaf evidence; your candidate remains provisional until then.

